# Comments

Keep code comments minimal. Do NOT add comments that just narrate what the code
does, restate the next line, or act as decorative section dividers. The code
should speak for itself.

Only add a comment when it explains non-obvious intent, a trade-off, a
constraint, or a "why" that isn't clear from the code.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — narration / dividers
// ---- helpers ----
// increment the counter
count += 1;
// Show the item as a loading placeholder, then fill it in later
items.push({ loading: true });

// ✅ GOOD — explains non-obvious why
// Bump a version token to bust the image cache; the edited file keeps the same URL.
setMediaVersion((v) => v + 1);
```

When editing existing files, prefer removing redundant comments over keeping
them. Do not narrate edits in code comments.
